    "result_text": "Full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the disposable-domain email blocklist rule for `POST /api/owners`.\n\nThe email-domain check fits naturally into the existing shared `OwnerEmail.normalize` helper, which both `ValidateOwnerFields` (POST) and `ValidateOwner` (PUT) already call, so both endpoints get the rule.\n\nChanges:\n- **`OwnerEmail.java`** \u2014 after syntactic validation and lower-casing, extract the domain and reject `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com` by throwing a new `DisposableOwnerEmailException`.\n- **`DisposableOwnerEmailException.java`** \u2014 new checked exception (per the AGENTS.md pattern: `extends Exception` so it surfaces in the `throws` clause).\n- **`DisposableOwnerEmailExceptionHandler.java`** + **escalation YAML** \u2014 responds `400` with `{\"errors\":[\"email\"]}`, mirroring the existing `InvalidOwnerEmailException` handler.\n- Added the new exception to the `throws` clauses of `ValidateOwnerFields` and `ValidateOwner`.\n\nThe rejection is distinct from the existing syntactic-invalid case (`InvalidOwnerEmailException`) so the two failure modes stay semantically separate, both mapping to 400.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsDisposableDomain` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).",
